  roomID: caida
  image: {fileID: -2523215614574402781, guid: ee1d54e32d460ff488fb2c767dfc42b7, type: 3}
  description:
  - "At the back of the caida stands a glass case set in a splendid and elegant Renaissance-style
    framework, possibly made by Ar\xE9valo. Inside is a religious scene rendered
    with extreme realism. "
  - "The display shows Our Lady of Peace and Prosperous Voyages, worshiped in Antipolo,
    visiting Capitana Inez while disguised as a beggar. \r\n"
  - "Capitana Inez is shown during her sickness, with yellow and bluish tones that
    make her appear almost like a decaying corpse. The figure is rendered with unsettling
    realism. \r\n"
  - "Glasses and other objects associated with a long illness surround Capitana Inez.
    They are reproduced so minutely that even their contents can be distinguished.
    \r\n"
